## Summary

The membership tier feature lives in the **PetClinic** Spring Boot app. The tier is a **derived (read-only) property computed on the `Owner` entity itself** (`getMembershipTier()`), populated indirectly from fields set during owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (namesakeCount, householdSize, email). It is exposed via the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` (schema defined in `openapi.yml`), mapped by MapStruct. A test (`AcceptanceTest`) wants it replaced with a numeric `membershipLevel`.

Note: `OwnerDto` is **generated at build time** from `openapi.yml` (no hand-written Java DTO exists; nothing is currently in `target/`). To change the response field you edit `openapi.yml`.

---

