## 4. DTO/response definition — `openapi.yml` (L2139-2157)

The `OwnerDto` Java class is generated from this schema. `membershipTier` is a read-only string:

```yaml
            namesakeCount:
              title: Namesake count
              description: >-
                The number of existing owners that, at the time this owner was
                created, already shared the same firstName and lastName
                (compared case-insensitively).
              type: integer
              format: int32
              minimum: 0
              example: 1
              readOnly: true
            membershipTier:
              title: Membership tier
              description: >-
                The owner's membership tier: 'SILVER' when namesakeCount is 0 and
                an email is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'.
              type: string
              example: 'SILVER'
              readOnly: true
```
(Note: this description is stale vs. the entity, which also adds a GOLD tier.)

Mapper: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — `OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);` (L21). MapStruct auto-maps `membershipTier` from the entity getter, so changing the field name requires matching names in both the entity and `openapi.yml`.

